Position: Junior Program Analyst with Security Clearance

h3&gt;

Junior Program Analyst with Security Clearance p&gt;

Be among the first 25 applicants. 3 days ago. p&gt;

Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) – Onsite:
Clarksburg, WV. h3&gt;

Position Overview p&gt;

En Pro Vera Corporation is actively seeking a Junior Program Analyst to support the FBI’s Criminal Justice Information Services (CJIS) Division in Clarksburg, WV. The role focuses on determining a person’s eligibility to possess firearms or explosives in accordance with federal law. The analyst will work in a fast‑paced, dynamic environment at the forefront of criminal‑justice technology. h3&gt;

Responsibilities p&gt;
• Ensure the accuracy of all processing and research in accordance with federally published guidelines. ul
• Conduct research on explosives permit checks and analyze information for validity.
• Research and analyze criminal backgrounds as part of Firearm Transactions, Explosives Permits, and other background checks.
• Report any point‑of‑contact changes to the appropriate personnel.
• Communicate with law‑enforcement agencies via fax, e‑mail, or phone and document communications.
• Evaluate existing procedures and provide recommended actions or solutions.
• Complete necessary document clean‑up of existing records to update and/or purge documentation as needed.h3&gt;

Required Skills and Experience p&gt;(See full job posting for complete information) ul
• Bachelor’s degree or a minimum of two (2) years of relevant experience.
• Attention to detail, oral communication, and interpersonal skills.
• Proficient computer skills, including Microsoft Office Suite and Google Chrome.
• Active Security Clearance – Secret.
• Ability to work multiple shifts including nights, weekends, and all holidays except Christmas.h3&gt;

Location p&gt;

Clarksburg, WV – onsite. h3&gt;

Compensation and Benefits p&gt;

Competitive salary and paid time off, including 11 government holidays. h3&gt;

About En Pro Vera p&gt;

En Pro Vera fosters an inclusive culture that values every employee and encourages collaboration. We prioritize veteran, service‑disabled veteran, and Native American applicants. h3&gt;

EEO Statement p&gt;

EEO is the Law – En Pro Vera pledges to treat all applicants with dignity and respect. The company will not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, ancestry, genetic information, veteran status, disability, or any other legally protected status. p&gt;

